{"files":[{"content":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <iterator>\n#include <string>\n\nnamespace\n{\nbool is_whitespace(char c)\n{\n    return (c == ' ')\n        || (c == '\\n')\n        || (c == '\\r')\n        || (c == '\\t')\n        || (c == '\\f')\n        || (c == '\\v');\n}\n\nclass BufferedOutput\n{\npublic:\n    BufferedOutput() : used_(0) {}\n\n    void append_permutation(std::string const& permutation)\n    {\n        append_pair('[', ' ');\n\n        char const* input = permutation.data();\n        std::size_t remaining = permutation.size();\n        while (remaining != 0) {\n            if (sizeof(buffer_) - used_ < 2) {\n                flush();\n            }\n\n            std::size_t const available_pairs =\n                (sizeof(buffer_) - used_) / 2;\n            std::size_t const count =\n                remaining < available_pairs ? remaining : available_pairs;\n            char* target = buffer_ + used_;\n            for (std::size_t i = 0; i != count; ++i) {\n                target[2 * i] = input[i];\n                target[2 * i + 1] = ' ';\n            }\n            used_ += count * 2;\n            input += count;\n            remaining -= count;\n        }\n\n        append_pair(']', '\\n');\n    }\n\n    void flush()\n    {\n        if (used_ != 0) {\n            std::cout.write(buffer_, static_cast<std::streamsize>(used_));\n            used_ = 0;\n        }\n    }\n\nprivate:\n    void append_pair(char first, char second)\n    {\n        if (sizeof(buffer_) - used_ < 2) {\n            flush();\n        }\n        buffer_[used_++] = first;\n        buffer_[used_++] = second;\n    }\n\n    char buffer_[64 * 1024];\n    std::size_t used_;\n};\n\nstd::string read_text_from_stdin()\n{\n    std::istreambuf_iterator<char> begin(std::cin);\n    std::istreambuf_iterator<char> end;\n    std::string text(begin, end);\n    text.erase(std::remove_if(text.begin(), text.end(), is_whitespace),\n               text.end());\n    return text;\n}\n\nvoid generate_permutations(std::string& text, BufferedOutput& output)\n{\n    if (text.empty()) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n    std::sort(text.begin(), text.end());\n    do {\n        output.append_permutation(text);\n    } while (std::next_permutation(text.begin(), text.end()));\n}\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    std::ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    std::string text = read_text_from_stdin();\n    BufferedOutput output;\n    generate_permutations(text, output);\n    output.flush();\n    std::cout.flush();\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/permutations.cc"}],"hypothesis":"A fixed-size output block removes the forced flush and small stream insertions per permutation; formatting character/space pairs directly into contiguous storage improves serialization locality without retaining factorial-sized output.","notes":"The 64 KiB staging buffer is reused and bounded. Explicit byte-counted writes preserve embedded non-C-string bytes, exact spacing, duplicate handling, and empty-input behavior.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace per-line std::endl output with a reusable 64 KiB C++ ostream staging buffer flushed in blocks.","Serialize each permutation through contiguous pairwise writes and use standard in-place lexicographic stepping to safely handle the terminal descending suffix."]}